# What a compute host runs besides our own binaries, pinned by version and
# SHA-256. lab/host-setup.sh, the host bundle's install.sh and CI read this
# file; change a pin here and nowhere else. Every value is checked after
# download, and a mismatch stops the install.
#
# Firecracker and its jailer: a release tarball from GitHub. A new release
# restores older memory images only if it reads their snapshot format; see
# docs/operations.md#upgrades before changing it.
#
# v1.17.0 is the first 1.17 release whose vsock takes host connections
# after a pause and resume (firecracker#6100, the hang in issue #6074),
# which every wake from paused relies on. Fixes after it that Opengeni compute
# does not wait for: #6208 (a guest connecting to a host socket whose
# accept queue is full stalls its VMM; guest ports are accepted at once and
# those beyond a cap closed) and #6237 (discarding part of a huge page;
# guests on huge pages report free memory in whole huge pages).
FC_VERSION=v1.17.0
FC_SHA256_X86_64=06094a1108ae9e82aa4c23a775aa92758f53f1175d422270d9d6162cb9ade558

# The guest kernel and the lab's root filesystem, from one Firecracker CI
# artifact set (Firecracker's own tested guest builds; the config is kept
# beside the kernel).
GUEST_ARTIFACTS=https://s3.amazonaws.com/spec.ccfc.min/firecracker-ci/20261016-5732b8331e1e-0/x86_64
GUEST_KERNEL=vmlinux-6.18.54
GUEST_KERNEL_SHA256=445b3d0ed9650869e854656308d60e6cca773190526b037b45941cbf61910f0d
GUEST_KERNEL_CONFIG_SHA256=7dbdc7445d01d3dd049b1e653534bde71266d59afaf9c1de50a8a6b8a8c138d0
LAB_ROOTFS=ubuntu-24.04.squashfs
LAB_ROOTFS_SHA256=40eaeb2ccd067314d75977784835884c22f19190b757456662df13134f58956e
